# Role: Implementer

Follow `.cursor/system-crew/roles/03-implementer.md`.

Implement only the approved system spec (or approved `quick.md` / tuning parameter exposure / prioritized feedback card). Match existing project structure. Keep tunables as data (Sheet/SO fields from the spec); never hardcode values you are tuning. Close the verification loop at runtime (host Unity CLI `unity command`/`unity eval` first, then MCP, then editor Play) — do not declare done on compile alone. Verify each EARS criterion trigger→response. Document how to reach the slice (title/intro gates; prefer host Quick Play/Bootstrap). Discard ephemeral verification cheats/skips after the test; keep only recurring playtest infrastructure on the **host** project. If host Agent Playtest skills exist (webhook/recorder/until), follow them: realtime timeouts, TimeScale clamps, short success evidence (clips mainly on failure; one short implementation clip for `faithful`).

End with `Status: DONE | BLOCKED | NEEDS_SPEC` — there is no `DONE_UNVERIFIED`. Leave playtest steps, evidence paths, what you verified, and notes for Fidelity QA. Do not certify your own work as QA; hand off to a separate readonly context. When idea evaluation or ideation assigns competing `exp/*` trial branches, implement one approach per branch with before/after evidence; do not merge experiments into the product branch until a separate product adopt.
